[{:db/id "q-8103/selection/44382dcc1631a06ceb8cbd80c6da739f2bf0a44e82da0d50be00a6ef84433eee" :answer/id #uuid "468cac85-0e6b-5c0c-b395-0e773de0d123" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{5x/2}+Bx{e}^{5x/2}+\\frac{2}{7}{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8103/selection/2b7f2f205a461846105b08f9145a0b927f1e4f4745ebc9392402cb8a2e577d9b" :answer/id #uuid "3530c584-6328-512b-adeb-a33287509755" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{5x/2}+Bx{e}^{5x/2}-\\frac{4}{49}{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8103/selection/571254a391555331e5a33d54807aedd5875b9d2ff3a24cc74c654deda7769082" :answer/id #uuid "81c681ec-4ff9-582e-91da-0ad08c942195" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{5x/2}+Bx{e}^{5x/2}+\\frac{16}{49}{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8103/selection/0978ff76ad1a338c0a6dc10ec9122353a423f7d66fa6ddb140f6332f359fffcb" :answer/id #uuid "095c6f84-a92f-5535-8684-c41d550e9a49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-5x/2}+B{e}^{5x/2}-\\frac{4}{7}{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8103/selection/1b36d7949b0bcc927f315cb627859712e93ffc935054d574e50510266aa71d28" :answer/id #uuid "8359288a-a3b2-55cc-98af-f290bc634e96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-5x/2}+B{e}^{5x/2}+\\frac{8}{49}{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8103/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fcff9fc4-517f-578a-b6f7-577b3359653b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8103/selection/571254a391555331e5a33d54807aedd5875b9d2ff3a24cc74c654deda7769082" :answer-field/choices ["q-8103/selection/44382dcc1631a06ceb8cbd80c6da739f2bf0a44e82da0d50be00a6ef84433eee" "q-8103/selection/2b7f2f205a461846105b08f9145a0b927f1e4f4745ebc9392402cb8a2e577d9b" "q-8103/selection/571254a391555331e5a33d54807aedd5875b9d2ff3a24cc74c654deda7769082" "q-8103/selection/0978ff76ad1a338c0a6dc10ec9122353a423f7d66fa6ddb140f6332f359fffcb" "q-8103/selection/1b36d7949b0bcc927f315cb627859712e93ffc935054d574e50510266aa71d28"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8103" :question/id #uuid "9c248c7e-6807-55f8-be03-cfefc78d425e" :question/math-academy-id "q-8103" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{25y}{4}=4{e}^{-x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{25y}{4}=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +\\frac{25}{4} & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda -\\frac{5}{2})}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}$ is a repeated root, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{5x/2}+Bx{e}^{5x/2}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $4{e}^{-x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $-1$, which is not the root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {e}^{-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-\\alpha {e}^{-x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha {e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha {e}^{-x}-5(-\\alpha {e}^{-x})+\\frac{25}{4}\\alpha {e}^{-x} & =4{e}^{-x} \\\\ (1+5+\\frac{25}{4})\\alpha {e}^{-x} & =4{e}^{-x} \\\\ \\frac{49}{4}\\alpha {e}^{-x} & =4{e}^{-x} \\\\ \\frac{49}{4}\\alpha  & =4 \\\\ \\alpha  & =\\frac{16}{49}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\frac{16}{49}{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{5x/2}+Bx{e}^{5x/2}+\\frac{16}{49}{e}^{-x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8103/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03260b0d-f1c4-5c40-89dc-3de2d1017148"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8103"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93675/selection/fcfc6ef199aa7b26c979bc185ff68cddbb6012a13ca0b629d7cee095d4e0f01e" :answer/id #uuid "fc52a848-2e6c-5455-ac1a-e2c9e0b33def" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=2x{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93675/selection/33faaac67d237830a34ff5708df9ba80f67a0246fbf0aa1252044167551afd81" :answer/id #uuid "f32a9e0d-f302-55c5-a5bd-fd6f0e760951" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}={e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93675/selection/fdc74ff8a4dd3e4928e35dd0024cb869f6a1869e84281d4faa80cef1b4c3d91e" :answer/id #uuid "a89a606f-d688-58ab-83b5-f801bf70308a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-2{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93675/selection/d9c6f406d51b68ad927e3e74512ffaf99490e33bbf2cacef3df5e2170e426204" :answer/id #uuid "d13580aa-7ff6-53b6-9113-5f2b3a26d41d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=3{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93675/selection/b72b8197a424e5349a35e8038b1ca8275471a08644b43897f0f377a70b9b3eb8" :answer/id #uuid "c73ad300-8c72-50f3-a6bc-13dedafd9a1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-3x{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93675/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "118bb02c-7b00-5095-ad27-28d4515c5668" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93675/selection/d9c6f406d51b68ad927e3e74512ffaf99490e33bbf2cacef3df5e2170e426204" :answer-field/choices ["q-93675/selection/fcfc6ef199aa7b26c979bc185ff68cddbb6012a13ca0b629d7cee095d4e0f01e" "q-93675/selection/33faaac67d237830a34ff5708df9ba80f67a0246fbf0aa1252044167551afd81" "q-93675/selection/fdc74ff8a4dd3e4928e35dd0024cb869f6a1869e84281d4faa80cef1b4c3d91e" "q-93675/selection/d9c6f406d51b68ad927e3e74512ffaf99490e33bbf2cacef3df5e2170e426204" "q-93675/selection/b72b8197a424e5349a35e8038b1ca8275471a08644b43897f0f377a70b9b3eb8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93675" :question/id #uuid "667003ae-52b1-572c-b234-cf239bc6b6d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-93675" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+8y=12{e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x),$ find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "Since the complementary function is ${y}_{c}(x)={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x),$ the roots of the auxiliary equation are $\\lambda =-2\\pm 2\\text{i}.$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $12{e}^{-2x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $-2$, which is not the root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {e}^{-2x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\alpha {e}^{-2x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=4\\alpha {e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\alpha {e}^{-2x}+4(-2\\alpha {e}^{-2x})+8(\\alpha {e}^{-2x}) & =12{e}^{-2x} \\\\ (4-8+8)\\alpha {e}^{-2x} & =12{e}^{-2x} \\\\ 4\\alpha {e}^{-2x} & =12{e}^{-2x} \\\\ \\alpha  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=3{e}^{-2x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93675/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03260b0d-f1c4-5c40-89dc-3de2d1017148"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93675"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64289/selection/df433e9dffef84febdee0c4dc10112c26b2f0f88ddddae52bfd61577c3cec384" :answer/id #uuid "488331d3-871b-5af2-8b4e-04f2d244fe72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=4{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64289/selection/7c3a3246c0993f63ebf58354660799c5228cbceee11f3bb42e729108bb3c80b0" :answer/id #uuid "70d59520-c2d1-5a4e-af9b-5ac668029bed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64289/selection/9c9ae1a9a016f081542b3d4c2be0973ed123310f309ca470c46015598a9b9a51" :answer/id #uuid "fbb8f278-50bb-5025-a754-dae70c45b38a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=2{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64289/selection/f6db6a947faf2bf20d440a465cd038703d398350c754dedef440a9fde50ad73d" :answer/id #uuid "40616a1d-e422-55f4-8121-95402df4f3c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64289/selection/9ce14500adf39c52dcae7889150a452df3f88ec9416fde64c897019043f44b76" :answer/id #uuid "b9e1832a-435f-5f76-873f-f51b72d74e2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-x{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64289/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0f319933-2af8-56cb-a1ab-c35ec7698680" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64289/selection/9c9ae1a9a016f081542b3d4c2be0973ed123310f309ca470c46015598a9b9a51" :answer-field/choices ["q-64289/selection/df433e9dffef84febdee0c4dc10112c26b2f0f88ddddae52bfd61577c3cec384" "q-64289/selection/7c3a3246c0993f63ebf58354660799c5228cbceee11f3bb42e729108bb3c80b0" "q-64289/selection/9c9ae1a9a016f081542b3d4c2be0973ed123310f309ca470c46015598a9b9a51" "q-64289/selection/f6db6a947faf2bf20d440a465cd038703d398350c754dedef440a9fde50ad73d" "q-64289/selection/9ce14500adf39c52dcae7889150a452df3f88ec9416fde64c897019043f44b76"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64289" :question/id #uuid "1057cfea-89cf-56ee-9a3c-493daedf6a35" :question/math-academy-id "q-64289" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-9\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+18y=8{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{3x}+B{e}^{6x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "Since the complementary function is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{3x}+B{e}^{6x},$ the roots of the auxiliary equation are $\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =6.$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $8{e}^{2x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $2$, which is not the root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {e}^{2x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha {e}^{2x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=4\\alpha {e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\alpha {e}^{2x}-9(2\\alpha {e}^{2x})+18(\\alpha {e}^{2x}) & =8{e}^{2x} \\\\ (4-18+18)\\alpha {e}^{2x} & =8{e}^{2x} \\\\ 4\\alpha {e}^{2x} & =8{e}^{2x} \\\\ \\alpha  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=2{e}^{2x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64289/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03260b0d-f1c4-5c40-89dc-3de2d1017148"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64289"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93673/selection/f435e306304b3338b79c848386719f31b3525a0663b0890e1f5a42d83e43154c" :answer/id #uuid "7d7c4e61-7b14-55cc-af2d-4870b6c16baf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-2{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93673/selection/75c4b6d5398f2d86a79b21f58712ef858d7b06924296b86b6232f61d929b4e8f" :answer/id #uuid "03bd4e83-74f7-5112-9a3f-a5c8dbf5f7a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=P{e}^{x}+Qx{e}^{x}+2{x}^{2}{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93673/selection/f40fb02adf272d3b6c39c891deaf8ea415061f931462c73551abcbb3fea603fe" :answer/id #uuid "17c67761-3b91-512a-86b1-1367e898ca83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+5x{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93673/selection/3d4788bf4ef666347339f4adede6ca7cb0904513afd81f500f991715bb488dc4" :answer/id #uuid "8c358ec7-bad2-5078-8751-207c568132f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93673/selection/2c43d798b3aaa06820168160b5104d31abfca7b8a6234458976be3d6bb3b3ed4" :answer/id #uuid "27dbdc82-7de0-5db3-a009-698a3082052e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=P{e}^{2x}+Q{e}^{-2x}-x{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93673/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1cfcb026-536c-5ba9-8c00-5b9c789ee138" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93673/selection/3d4788bf4ef666347339f4adede6ca7cb0904513afd81f500f991715bb488dc4" :answer-field/choices ["q-93673/selection/f435e306304b3338b79c848386719f31b3525a0663b0890e1f5a42d83e43154c" "q-93673/selection/75c4b6d5398f2d86a79b21f58712ef858d7b06924296b86b6232f61d929b4e8f" "q-93673/selection/f40fb02adf272d3b6c39c891deaf8ea415061f931462c73551abcbb3fea603fe" "q-93673/selection/3d4788bf4ef666347339f4adede6ca7cb0904513afd81f500f991715bb488dc4" "q-93673/selection/2c43d798b3aaa06820168160b5104d31abfca7b8a6234458976be3d6bb3b3ed4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93673" :question/id #uuid "a50bb5dc-9198-5fcf-9e92-5a19a3bdc9f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-93673" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5y=20{e}^{4x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5y=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +5=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +5 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4)-4+5 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda -2 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =2\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c}(x) & ={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $20{e}^{4x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $4$, which is not the root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {e}^{4x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=4\\alpha {e}^{4x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=16\\alpha {e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16\\alpha {e}^{4x}-4(4\\alpha {e}^{4x})+5(\\alpha {e}^{4x}) & =20{e}^{4x} \\\\ (16-16+5)\\alpha {e}^{4x} & =20{e}^{4x} \\\\ 5\\alpha {e}^{4x} & =20{e}^{4x} \\\\ 5\\alpha  & =20 \\\\ \\alpha  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=4{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{e}^{4x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93673/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03260b0d-f1c4-5c40-89dc-3de2d1017148"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93673"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64290"] :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4y={e}^{-3x}\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{-4x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "Since the complementary function is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{-4x},$ the roots of the auxiliary equation are $\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =-4.$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is ${e}^{-3x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $-3$, which is not the root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {e}^{-3x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\alpha {e}^{-3x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=9\\alpha {e}^{-3x}\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9\\alpha {e}^{-3x}+3(-3\\alpha {e}^{-3x})-4(\\alpha {e}^{-3x}) & ={e}^{-3x} \\\\ (9-9-4)\\alpha {e}^{-3x} & ={e}^{-3x} \\\\ -4\\alpha {e}^{-3x} & ={e}^{-3x} \\\\ \\alpha  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-3x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-93678/selection/d2ee92642d9f7c31920486cc73717f4620d039a893c28f56c0976182e11e45be" :answer/id #uuid "ca65ff4c-5e5b-5f0e-bf09-9e0aac2e92b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-2x{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93678/selection/c30adf39dd2f9912498cdfbd4613ddb935f1c1f9c8d9433ea7da2bd3e81e999d" :answer/id #uuid "deb13f75-d58b-5e27-8aeb-dbd87db5306a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-5{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93678/selection/b302b7041ab525246648d51c6e6892f4c671a2378f814f656416b2b2cf0fd8e1" :answer/id #uuid "68e9496f-8192-5133-aeed-6e67dcdd2768" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-5x{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93678/selection/6b439ffba3c73fccf60b0a0a2420969a0d96a5d7ece8a3e8ad82d6bcf0296416" :answer/id #uuid "af738071-c5ad-51f1-b3eb-08cf75db9ab7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=x{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93678/selection/6b3f64ec4abc1dab9c62b88e8053031067f25eddde20943c6e07a82ff5578bad" :answer/id #uuid "88c0c6ad-19b0-5966-8897-6ce8400587be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=2{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93678/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b33b88c-0891-56ce-b86d-62e75dafbb2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93678/selection/d2ee92642d9f7c31920486cc73717f4620d039a893c28f56c0976182e11e45be" :answer-field/choices ["q-93678/selection/d2ee92642d9f7c31920486cc73717f4620d039a893c28f56c0976182e11e45be" "q-93678/selection/c30adf39dd2f9912498cdfbd4613ddb935f1c1f9c8d9433ea7da2bd3e81e999d" "q-93678/selection/b302b7041ab525246648d51c6e6892f4c671a2378f814f656416b2b2cf0fd8e1" "q-93678/selection/6b439ffba3c73fccf60b0a0a2420969a0d96a5d7ece8a3e8ad82d6bcf0296416" "q-93678/selection/6b3f64ec4abc1dab9c62b88e8053031067f25eddde20943c6e07a82ff5578bad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93678" :question/id #uuid "0b0d7eeb-30c2-58fb-b039-5edb4ff9136a" :question/math-academy-id "q-93678" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4y=10{e}^{-x}\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{4x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "Since the complementary function is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{4x},$ the roots of the auxiliary equation are $\\lambda =-1$ and $\\lambda =4.$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $10{e}^{-x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $-1$, which coincides with one of the roots of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha x{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha (1-x){e}^{-x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha (x-2){e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (x-2){e}^{-x}-3(\\alpha (1-x){e}^{-x})-4(\\alpha x{e}^{-x}) & =10{e}^{-x} \\\\ (x-2-3+3x-4x)\\alpha {e}^{-x} & =10{e}^{-x} \\\\ -5\\alpha {e}^{-x} & =10{e}^{-x} \\\\ -5\\alpha  & =10 \\\\ \\alpha  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-2x{e}^{-x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93678/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61611329-9ecd-5917-a11e-3b5effa69673"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93678"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93682/selection/ef29208c4d8ee953645dc23f9244f7efcd09ac3de1c4b8eb4295ecb2865cfcc0" :answer/id #uuid "c906e411-411c-5ef4-b71b-5a5fff5f7bac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-x}+2x{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93682/selection/dce88f33c90ebac90e611fdee56846ac07d0390dca0b05a460dca4cdd0fccea8" :answer/id #uuid "10c520ce-4e99-5622-87e1-84c05293c970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-x}-x{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93682/selection/5ade85cac188b50f4ff713e591ce47c4265fa140e72a73c81b4a3a2d6dc46bc2" :answer/id #uuid "c03ae583-3a64-517a-a2cd-e77866f10014" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{x}-4{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93682/selection/4aaf00913adda9c51c50a26ee36488812aac7d10517571ca7fa2b2a76a6b9cd1" :answer/id #uuid "20ce795d-937f-5cc5-96cc-961b233e248c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93682/selection/4229191900c8e3c50c3c3e8c1f31b58ccacb20acc96d18c4f94e2c19aaffa4e9" :answer/id #uuid "fe78f13e-877f-5b48-a1bc-e7089c8ccbd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-x}+4x{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93682/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d196286f-5f47-55b2-a2e4-6fbd9252c511" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93682/selection/4229191900c8e3c50c3c3e8c1f31b58ccacb20acc96d18c4f94e2c19aaffa4e9" :answer-field/choices ["q-93682/selection/ef29208c4d8ee953645dc23f9244f7efcd09ac3de1c4b8eb4295ecb2865cfcc0" "q-93682/selection/dce88f33c90ebac90e611fdee56846ac07d0390dca0b05a460dca4cdd0fccea8" "q-93682/selection/5ade85cac188b50f4ff713e591ce47c4265fa140e72a73c81b4a3a2d6dc46bc2" "q-93682/selection/4aaf00913adda9c51c50a26ee36488812aac7d10517571ca7fa2b2a76a6b9cd1" "q-93682/selection/4229191900c8e3c50c3c3e8c1f31b58ccacb20acc96d18c4f94e2c19aaffa4e9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93682" :question/id #uuid "8c365de3-c119-52dd-962e-42c6ad6481e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-93682" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=4{e}^{-x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +1) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-2$ or $\\lambda =-1$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $4{e}^{-x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $-1$, which coincides with one of the roots of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha x{e}^{-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha (1-x){e}^{-x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha (x-2){e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (x-2){e}^{-x}+3(\\alpha (1-x){e}^{-x})+2(\\alpha x{e}^{-x}) & =4{e}^{-x} \\\\ (x-2+3-3x+2x)\\alpha {e}^{-x} & =4{e}^{-x} \\\\ \\alpha {e}^{-x} & =4{e}^{-x} \\\\ \\alpha  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=4x{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-x}+4x{e}^{-x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93682/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61611329-9ecd-5917-a11e-3b5effa69673"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93682"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-93683"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=4{e}^{3x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-1$ or $\\lambda =3$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $4{e}^{3x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $3$, which coincides with one of the roots of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha x{e}^{3x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha (1+3x){e}^{3x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha (9x+6){e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (9x+6){e}^{3x}-2(\\alpha (1+3x){e}^{3x})-3(\\alpha x{e}^{3x}) & =4{e}^{3x} \\\\ (9x+6-2-6x-3x)\\alpha {e}^{3x} & =4{e}^{3x} \\\\ 4\\alpha {e}^{3x} & =4{e}^{3x} \\\\ 4\\alpha  & =4 \\\\ \\alpha  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{3x}+x{e}^{3x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-64292/selection/530b8a1035c327c1dd24d5808467d3703667e37faca9495e56c29d877a4847a3" :answer/id #uuid "c03c4a47-5261-540d-a442-0ed71ce78af0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=2x{e}^{-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64292/selection/8e96303ff46cacc857a96bd5437b46570343f39e3de6740e5e65eaf220c27abe" :answer/id #uuid "e35fa4a3-9020-5999-814d-5380dc95b75f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-3x{e}^{-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64292/selection/522397be6403437542f71513c4d6273a16d70b241ab2cb15d62490c55e7f9b37" :answer/id #uuid "d1b52098-f7bc-5008-9972-71c0b48c9e77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-x{e}^{-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64292/selection/62a599680d31465635264bbad32929e80077b09e9ecb8a4997523f87368da0aa" :answer/id #uuid "a7420652-c3f5-5039-b913-f13b6531491c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=3{e}^{-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64292/selection/b3904693581638b375de30b79fe8e33077b9ee3a9861a59944578ce6b0c72716" :answer/id #uuid "3a880f9e-da70-5bf4-9cd8-abb69eccf275" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-2{e}^{-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64292/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2957d7f6-2087-533f-8da9-8b91b8845792" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64292/selection/522397be6403437542f71513c4d6273a16d70b241ab2cb15d62490c55e7f9b37" :answer-field/choices ["q-64292/selection/530b8a1035c327c1dd24d5808467d3703667e37faca9495e56c29d877a4847a3" "q-64292/selection/8e96303ff46cacc857a96bd5437b46570343f39e3de6740e5e65eaf220c27abe" "q-64292/selection/522397be6403437542f71513c4d6273a16d70b241ab2cb15d62490c55e7f9b37" "q-64292/selection/62a599680d31465635264bbad32929e80077b09e9ecb8a4997523f87368da0aa" "q-64292/selection/b3904693581638b375de30b79fe8e33077b9ee3a9861a59944578ce6b0c72716"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64292" :question/id #uuid "f55c38ad-8baa-564e-9bec-31da8339ebdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-64292" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+6\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+8y=2{e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-4x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "Since the complementary function is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-4x},$ the roots of the auxiliary equation are $\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =-4.$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $2{e}^{-4x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $-4$, which coincides with one of the roots of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha x{e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha (1-4x){e}^{-4x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha (16x-8){e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (16x-8){e}^{-4x}+6(\\alpha (1-4x){e}^{-4x})+8(\\alpha x{e}^{-4x}) & =2{e}^{-4x} \\\\ (16x-8+6-24x+8x)\\alpha {e}^{-4x} & =2{e}^{-4x} \\\\ -2\\alpha {e}^{-4x} & =2{e}^{-4x} \\\\ -2\\alpha  & =2 \\\\ \\alpha  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-x{e}^{-4x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64292/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61611329-9ecd-5917-a11e-3b5effa69673"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64292"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93680/selection/decef6c7471ee729d2a5d04c50260f3511f696f19e0f1cbc0b8fc4ca37b29a71" :answer/id #uuid "41e6dde8-59bf-59c6-828c-d218d6abac81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-3x}+2{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93680/selection/a10f92b899ec06d55a82f04236f7f8e556013999aac1a03a74aba3c45833248c" :answer/id #uuid "90cef367-d458-55c6-b7d0-db4e2db7f145" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{3x}-x{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93680/selection/2d1d460f882d7bfd536c987dec09906ad0cc08138d2721e960ae14ba742e9007" :answer/id #uuid "22944d33-8918-5daa-8d7d-8cdeae652384" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{3x}+6x{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93680/selection/40a01b3bb32b85e66428075ccfa961c58336ccf748218ced3cf2f01b51df8b86" :answer/id #uuid "32a30ef0-463c-56f1-b049-679c9146e394" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{3x}-3{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93680/selection/73ea3ffb2510b7a62c28c10cc99438e1d71b06ac80f4ddb430c8e8b1f952930b" :answer/id #uuid "22efc29d-b776-5b46-9a4b-a8541e740a2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{3x}+3x{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93680/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "86b85751-4127-53cb-9888-a7cfaa5f9bd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93680/selection/2d1d460f882d7bfd536c987dec09906ad0cc08138d2721e960ae14ba742e9007" :answer-field/choices ["q-93680/selection/decef6c7471ee729d2a5d04c50260f3511f696f19e0f1cbc0b8fc4ca37b29a71" "q-93680/selection/a10f92b899ec06d55a82f04236f7f8e556013999aac1a03a74aba3c45833248c" "q-93680/selection/2d1d460f882d7bfd536c987dec09906ad0cc08138d2721e960ae14ba742e9007" "q-93680/selection/40a01b3bb32b85e66428075ccfa961c58336ccf748218ced3cf2f01b51df8b86" "q-93680/selection/73ea3ffb2510b7a62c28c10cc99438e1d71b06ac80f4ddb430c8e8b1f952930b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93680" :question/id #uuid "feda8138-bd1a-5735-8f46-9588cc9d6c9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-93680" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6y=6{e}^{3x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +6 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =2$ or $\\lambda =3$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $6{e}^{3x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $3$, which coincides with one of the roots of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha x{e}^{3x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha (1+3x){e}^{3x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha (9x+6){e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p}$, ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (9x+6){e}^{3x}-5(\\alpha (1+3x){e}^{3x})+6(\\alpha x{e}^{3x}) & =6{e}^{3x} \\\\ (9x+6-5-15x+6x)\\alpha {e}^{3x} & =6{e}^{3x} \\\\ \\alpha {e}^{3x} & =6{e}^{3x} \\\\ \\alpha  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=6x{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{3x}+6x{e}^{3x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93680/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61611329-9ecd-5917-a11e-3b5effa69673"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93680"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64294/selection/901e500b1fd0f35d6ab5d7d0f6859802ee42ecd4d95faec8e8950fb0c0e1e3cc" :answer/id #uuid "30dd42aa-9f7e-5c91-accb-9e3ae0b9d6c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=3x{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64294/selection/f6db6a947faf2bf20d440a465cd038703d398350c754dedef440a9fde50ad73d" :answer/id #uuid "53d6dd22-0578-5b24-9c4c-65fb7162c89e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64294/selection/049750fe247485fb83c9b086413edc29e9f406bb8364c4217aee6bea8d7aad76" :answer/id #uuid "6004929b-450c-507b-bedb-43dd04ccb911" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64294/selection/dfe1e5ed8cc71924ea4922c9c5e1e7e6e9ff00877954cd756d95015472aed5c1" :answer/id #uuid "d852390a-64c2-5027-97fa-e79ef3533177" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=2{x}^{2}{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64294/selection/e5e636be789ffedcda4d2513a88d3ea500d331bf002b5870b3ae5756473ee77c" :answer/id #uuid "7da87c26-752d-54f6-9002-89434bc27e6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64294/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2dbed1a-794c-51fe-86d4-c0ecfe6478b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64294/selection/e5e636be789ffedcda4d2513a88d3ea500d331bf002b5870b3ae5756473ee77c" :answer-field/choices ["q-64294/selection/901e500b1fd0f35d6ab5d7d0f6859802ee42ecd4d95faec8e8950fb0c0e1e3cc" "q-64294/selection/f6db6a947faf2bf20d440a465cd038703d398350c754dedef440a9fde50ad73d" "q-64294/selection/049750fe247485fb83c9b086413edc29e9f406bb8364c4217aee6bea8d7aad76" "q-64294/selection/dfe1e5ed8cc71924ea4922c9c5e1e7e6e9ff00877954cd756d95015472aed5c1" "q-64294/selection/e5e636be789ffedcda4d2513a88d3ea500d331bf002b5870b3ae5756473ee77c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64294" :question/id #uuid "9111b9e4-c234-557d-b1f8-8c4096c02984" :question/math-academy-id "q-64294" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=3{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{2x}+Bx{e}^{2x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "Since the complementary function is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{2x}+Bx{e}^{2x},$ we have that $\\lambda =2$ is the double root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $3{e}^{2x}.$  In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $2$, which coincides with the double root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{2x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha (2{x}^{2}+2x){e}^{2x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha (4{x}^{2}+8x+2){e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (4{x}^{2}+8x+2){e}^{2x}-4(\\alpha (2{x}^{2}+2x){e}^{2x})+4(\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{2x}) & =3{e}^{2x} \\\\ (4{x}^{2}+8x+2-8{x}^{2}-8x+4{x}^{2})\\alpha {e}^{2x} & =3{e}^{2x} \\\\ 2\\alpha {e}^{2x} & =3{e}^{2x} \\\\ 2\\alpha  & =3 \\\\ \\alpha  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}{e}^{2x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64294/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c01e7705-e8a6-5712-ad9a-2fc77ee3cdec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64294"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93687/selection/88552940a8eafbed01417f3aeac96db6bae3732675d8332ac5d34a6d3c4c94e5" :answer/id #uuid "c8b07144-0294-56f8-9285-1cb3ec7d8c5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-4{x}^{2}{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93687/selection/e5a5dcb4b98638ce4f0cc12ce567a571c5cbca2f997eb5a1a1ab8f52742b64ed" :answer/id #uuid "c0290b0c-7ec0-5540-8e4b-75d9ee2e797f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=4{x}^{2}{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93687/selection/816d0232802bab82395a3cddcdf4f45e2f121b4c0e56bffb2b35e2f230f31876" :answer/id #uuid "dd3b7c3e-4ad4-5d57-b949-d149be5d35ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=x{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93687/selection/bf7c3d74c10675e272ba729122f75a6458866139a6fcd4672a4ff6a1576550dc" :answer/id #uuid "08648012-10ed-5661-be6e-35987d836c58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=2{x}^{2}{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93687/selection/2ed3e763a51a0c9fabe909693eb1eb52063ce54595020452f2d075879b02f1bd" :answer/id #uuid "35c50590-2cc3-56d0-91d3-7e6a960981e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-2x{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93687/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6daf7e12-a358-5654-ad7e-8544adbf1a49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93687/selection/bf7c3d74c10675e272ba729122f75a6458866139a6fcd4672a4ff6a1576550dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-93687/selection/88552940a8eafbed01417f3aeac96db6bae3732675d8332ac5d34a6d3c4c94e5" "q-93687/selection/e5a5dcb4b98638ce4f0cc12ce567a571c5cbca2f997eb5a1a1ab8f52742b64ed" "q-93687/selection/816d0232802bab82395a3cddcdf4f45e2f121b4c0e56bffb2b35e2f230f31876" "q-93687/selection/bf7c3d74c10675e272ba729122f75a6458866139a6fcd4672a4ff6a1576550dc" "q-93687/selection/2ed3e763a51a0c9fabe909693eb1eb52063ce54595020452f2d075879b02f1bd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93687" :question/id #uuid "9bdcc65d-ace5-50fe-a859-cbc9e6149544" :question/math-academy-id "q-93687" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+10\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+25y=4{e}^{-5x}\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-5x}+Bx{e}^{-5x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "Since the complementary function is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-5x}+Bx{e}^{-5x},$ we have that $\\lambda =-5$ is the double root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $4{e}^{-5x}.$  In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $-5$, which coincides with the double root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{-5x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha (2x-5{x}^{2}){e}^{-5x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha (25{x}^{2}-20x+2){e}^{-5x}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (25{x}^{2}-20x+2){e}^{-5x}+10(\\alpha (2x-5{x}^{2}){e}^{-5x})+25(\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{-5x}) & =4{e}^{-5x} \\\\ (25{x}^{2}-20x+2+20x-50{x}^{2}+25{x}^{2})\\alpha {e}^{-5x} & =4{e}^{-5x} \\\\ 2\\alpha {e}^{-5x} & =4{e}^{-5x} \\\\ 2\\alpha  & =4 \\\\ \\alpha  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=2{x}^{2}{e}^{-5x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93687/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c01e7705-e8a6-5712-ad9a-2fc77ee3cdec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93687"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8102/selection/b821bb922da28faf010ad553192ae4b5f066b67e1ca98bd49c7d6e32f8fb23f5" :answer/id #uuid "04b775c9-bf23-50c9-bcb5-2c64b2b1bd28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{3x/2}+B{e}^{-3x/2}+2x{e}^{3x/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8102/selection/b63a40af2f123cad876626ac100553ddbd8575d7a9502a8724371a309868e865" :answer/id #uuid "9a8cb1a9-1aaf-5fec-95b8-31d79689847e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x/2}+B{e}^{-x/2}+{e}^{3x/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8102/selection/5eb69266fbfebbe3a2e405d1c43045801f3369bfa6820bc33dce0c80b4a24934" :answer/id #uuid "43d82bf4-c46a-5160-9e87-608da6ee4d67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{3x/2}+Bx{e}^{3x/2}+{x}^{2}{e}^{3x/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8102/selection/cbc3fd4f0d670df3cb678cced36b6880af9a6ba6ef0ddeafab2a5a972f90da0f" :answer/id #uuid "3495db7a-4b13-57d5-b796-6dadbc8677a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{3x/2}+Bx{e}^{3x/2}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{3x/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8102/selection/27919c8000c37a674488bd90bccda7de3d98056e2624f6b46c53852586856ab7" :answer/id #uuid "ef37b2f1-dfb8-5a6d-9bc4-8e857188fbf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{3x/2}+Bx{e}^{3x/2}-{x}^{2}{e}^{3x/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8102/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e77ab864-53e2-5c19-96d1-080ffaeb79f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8102/selection/cbc3fd4f0d670df3cb678cced36b6880af9a6ba6ef0ddeafab2a5a972f90da0f" :answer-field/choices ["q-8102/selection/b821bb922da28faf010ad553192ae4b5f066b67e1ca98bd49c7d6e32f8fb23f5" "q-8102/selection/b63a40af2f123cad876626ac100553ddbd8575d7a9502a8724371a309868e865" "q-8102/selection/5eb69266fbfebbe3a2e405d1c43045801f3369bfa6820bc33dce0c80b4a24934" "q-8102/selection/cbc3fd4f0d670df3cb678cced36b6880af9a6ba6ef0ddeafab2a5a972f90da0f" "q-8102/selection/27919c8000c37a674488bd90bccda7de3d98056e2624f6b46c53852586856ab7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8102" :question/id #uuid "3a5802fd-37fc-583e-8254-281bf6bcccd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-8102" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{9}{4}y=6{e}^{3x/2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{9}{4}y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +\\frac{9}{4} & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda -\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =\\frac{3}{2}$ is a repeated root, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{3x/2}+Bx{e}^{3x/2}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $6{e}^{3x/2}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $\\frac{3}{2}$, which coincides with the double root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{3x/2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha (2x+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}){e}^{3x/2},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha (2+6x+\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}){e}^{3x/2}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (2+6x+\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}){e}^{3x/2}-3(\\alpha (2x+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}){e}^{3x/2})+\\frac{9}{4}(\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{3x/2}) & =6{e}^{3x/2} \\\\ (2+6x+\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}-6x-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2})\\alpha {e}^{3x/2} & =6{e}^{3x/2} \\\\ 2\\alpha {e}^{3x/2} & =6{e}^{3x/2} \\\\ 2\\alpha  & =6 \\\\ \\alpha  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=3{x}^{2}{e}^{3x/2}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{3x/2}+Bx{e}^{3x/2}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{3x/2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8102/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c01e7705-e8a6-5712-ad9a-2fc77ee3cdec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8102"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93686/selection/2dec7663fe429034b2417c766b2b4a9e560b82d6cadf05ec8ef926dd3b3002e6" :answer/id #uuid "d16042df-1fc8-55f6-9a6f-8e9801cac98e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-2{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93686/selection/eda7f761ee11623a8365a7d6144b64cb04b3bce05981e4d0c45479aaefbfb5be" :answer/id #uuid "45af9035-4904-5cfe-80fb-6dcbb08b123a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-3x{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93686/selection/dfa094e70e190b2f241471fec9cad67a8db580418f61715f6972442cb9fb1499" :answer/id #uuid "4fcdaebb-ff1d-51f5-b3f7-72d73eeefb28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-2{x}^{2}{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93686/selection/f1ce430c5f5445ca6979df2cfc116d47f756fbee9bef2b42cbe6b78c0a43e605" :answer/id #uuid "c590d0dd-1711-5f33-9c20-33b1e0ed6602" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=x{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93686/selection/c7730ae35a98135d9d18831220445dcd43dfcb665dd9536c12ef017bb1b16d42" :answer/id #uuid "6f8afba0-184c-59b2-a7da-f48853bcd2eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=3{x}^{2}{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93686/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "62adf584-d6fd-5005-9fca-95d7054fdecd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93686/selection/c7730ae35a98135d9d18831220445dcd43dfcb665dd9536c12ef017bb1b16d42" :answer-field/choices ["q-93686/selection/2dec7663fe429034b2417c766b2b4a9e560b82d6cadf05ec8ef926dd3b3002e6" "q-93686/selection/eda7f761ee11623a8365a7d6144b64cb04b3bce05981e4d0c45479aaefbfb5be" "q-93686/selection/dfa094e70e190b2f241471fec9cad67a8db580418f61715f6972442cb9fb1499" "q-93686/selection/f1ce430c5f5445ca6979df2cfc116d47f756fbee9bef2b42cbe6b78c0a43e605" "q-93686/selection/c7730ae35a98135d9d18831220445dcd43dfcb665dd9536c12ef017bb1b16d42"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93686" :question/id #uuid "ec1ebe33-0bb3-5ea6-a15e-48fad1ecf313" :question/math-academy-id "q-93686" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+6\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+9y=6{e}^{-3x}\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-3x}+Bx{e}^{-3x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "Since the complementary function is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-3x}+Bx{e}^{-3x},$ we have that $\\lambda =-3$ is the double root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $6{e}^{-3x}.$  In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $-3$, which coincides with the double root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{-3x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha (2x-3{x}^{2}){e}^{-3x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha (9{x}^{2}-12x+2){e}^{-3x}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (9{x}^{2}-12x+2){e}^{-3x}+6(\\alpha (2x-3{x}^{2}){e}^{-3x})+9(\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{-3x}) & =6{e}^{-3x} \\\\ (9{x}^{2}-12x+2+12x-18{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2})\\alpha {e}^{-3x} & =6{e}^{-3x} \\\\ 2\\alpha {e}^{-3x} & =6{e}^{-3x} \\\\ 2\\alpha  & =6 \\\\ \\alpha  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=3{x}^{2}{e}^{-3x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93686/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c01e7705-e8a6-5712-ad9a-2fc77ee3cdec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93686"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93689/selection/91d667c62617232c91ff56d5e507eb82c0b8085f73d17bddd99a719b2ffb9e38" :answer/id #uuid "9fa2d155-fe84-570f-9367-4d597acd1fad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+Bx{e}^{-2x}+2{x}^{2}{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93689/selection/8431c2048390a508f6f902717258ff7b210fcd7e1c16bb9b90f07f8786903bae" :answer/id #uuid "4b653edc-78e8-5ab8-a710-d8176c5513e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{2x}-x{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93689/selection/26775ae54779bf9efbb5adb26e40fe166088f7bf694b5add307c1977b731b1fa" :answer/id #uuid "ce4f1de3-58e6-5672-9ec1-6461caa7fe83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{2x}+3x{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93689/selection/f02b5d7ab044656dee9aee0077dcc4a2d891332ee0b73c37b92f24a1428a6d28" :answer/id #uuid "0c9aec8f-8670-572b-a478-b9995c029df6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{2x}+4x{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93689/selection/5534b0c0de9f06a9982309176823eb5dafa004775a13ce19de1c96d163fc9ddb" :answer/id #uuid "f0a28033-3c1e-5ee6-bf76-ffd508fbdc56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+Bx{e}^{-2x}-4{x}^{2}{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93689/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "989ddf36-9815-5d7a-8094-6347081cf20e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93689/selection/91d667c62617232c91ff56d5e507eb82c0b8085f73d17bddd99a719b2ffb9e38" :answer-field/choices ["q-93689/selection/91d667c62617232c91ff56d5e507eb82c0b8085f73d17bddd99a719b2ffb9e38" "q-93689/selection/8431c2048390a508f6f902717258ff7b210fcd7e1c16bb9b90f07f8786903bae" "q-93689/selection/26775ae54779bf9efbb5adb26e40fe166088f7bf694b5add307c1977b731b1fa" "q-93689/selection/f02b5d7ab044656dee9aee0077dcc4a2d891332ee0b73c37b92f24a1428a6d28" "q-93689/selection/5534b0c0de9f06a9982309176823eb5dafa004775a13ce19de1c96d163fc9ddb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93689" :question/id #uuid "1b1ac2a7-38c5-50ac-b0e1-9c8eb0787f12" :question/math-academy-id "q-93689" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=4{e}^{-2x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-2$ is a repeated root, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-2x}+Bx{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $4{e}^{-2x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $-2$, which coincides with the double root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{-2x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =\\alpha (2x-2{x}^{2}){e}^{-2x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha (4{x}^{2}-8x+2){e}^{-2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (4{x}^{2}-8x+2){e}^{-2x}+4\\alpha (2x-2{x}^{2}){e}^{-2x}+4\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{-2x} & =4{e}^{-2x} \\\\ \\alpha (4{x}^{2}-8x+2+8x-8{x}^{2}+4{x}^{2}){e}^{-2x} & =4{e}^{-2x} \\\\ 2\\alpha {e}^{-2x} & =4{e}^{-2x} \\\\ 2\\alpha  & =4 \\\\ \\alpha  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=2{x}^{2}{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+Bx{e}^{-2x}+2{x}^{2}{e}^{-2x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93689/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c01e7705-e8a6-5712-ad9a-2fc77ee3cdec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93689"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93692/selection/d4cb04225c0f23f82fea69b5479b7b99b337426a84a15b9b0b05c02d4a9fdc6d" :answer/id #uuid "aa96c2f8-08c4-5858-bed7-d22a2a878ce0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-3x}+3{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93692/selection/93bf699e66ffece8518753c7dbc9d8c8a4a9b06a42ca2934f647c1e0f0b2e278" :answer/id #uuid "b1a59840-5572-57e4-9107-3d8dc820e936" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3{e}^{-3x}+{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93692/selection/971c6fcd97580f44e8654b0caff231a1ec1a9705fa3531f19a80ff8aabaa457d" :answer/id #uuid "ea926e9b-8273-529b-b8e6-17ae0b92d0d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93692/selection/14c5c77f580641d6d59df268760a79ffa14936296c4068f02b24b0e2a1b67357" :answer/id #uuid "39380810-f9f9-5386-a77c-1b5efc87dafb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4{e}^{-3x}+2x{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93692/selection/15d1746cef4afe32a2e27b71241d81aa29d423918b7b612a4c6685456351c0bd" :answer/id #uuid "04e3d8df-0284-53c5-b2c5-2e7fb66ead6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-3x}+2{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93692/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8333d15e-ba6f-56a5-a30e-d66d448a2056" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93692/selection/d4cb04225c0f23f82fea69b5479b7b99b337426a84a15b9b0b05c02d4a9fdc6d" :answer-field/choices ["q-93692/selection/d4cb04225c0f23f82fea69b5479b7b99b337426a84a15b9b0b05c02d4a9fdc6d" "q-93692/selection/93bf699e66ffece8518753c7dbc9d8c8a4a9b06a42ca2934f647c1e0f0b2e278" "q-93692/selection/971c6fcd97580f44e8654b0caff231a1ec1a9705fa3531f19a80ff8aabaa457d" "q-93692/selection/14c5c77f580641d6d59df268760a79ffa14936296c4068f02b24b0e2a1b67357" "q-93692/selection/15d1746cef4afe32a2e27b71241d81aa29d423918b7b612a4c6685456351c0bd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93692" :question/id #uuid "a2c64f62-0e70-5fc9-810e-3f87da8d1c55" :question/math-academy-id "q-93692" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=8{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(x)=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=8{e}^{x},\\,y(0)=4,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=4$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =A{e}^{-3(0)}+B{e}^{0}+2(0){e}^{0} \\\\ 4 & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}+2{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=2$ into the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =-3A{e}^{-3(0)}+B{e}^{0}+2(0){e}^{0}+2{e}^{0} \\\\ 2 & =-3A+B+2 \\\\ 0 & =-3A+B \\\\ B & =3A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=4 \\\\ B=3A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=1,B=3.$\n\nFinally, since $A=1$ and $B=3,$ we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-3x}+3{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93692/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "749a2a49-4181-5be7-b5ef-3e5f8d82219f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93692"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93840/selection/dfa228bf3eb066b1b38aa83c5d04b6f7393e470663ace6a5123a0e7c76cef8f3" :answer/id #uuid "d4d6bb53-9f20-5256-a4a0-29bc2c5f24f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{e}^{x}-2{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93840/selection/10e187ac029f78b83799d5ef21c84839ff17365a8e1dd17d9e1406697e8da9d6" :answer/id #uuid "c7a4ca0f-1477-5bcd-9f14-b65f20f6b290" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-x}-3x{e}^{-x}-2{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93840/selection/60693dc123e7d308b27dc6cf4a82a6c74f361da754e33fe63c7ec26320871b29" :answer/id #uuid "086760f0-4c66-5ce3-a6b1-c985aa20f259" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4x{e}^{x}-2{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93840/selection/b2faf1ca059239c75b27e85c9643ddc4144a7d6daf577ac4beb6f0db9ab7fbab" :answer/id #uuid "360c12e3-99d3-5277-a391-e597d2dc5185" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}-2{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93840/selection/a86345bd9c6764497c7636561836dc928800e1ed8eafbc0dbb5fabacff26a9de" :answer/id #uuid "41f9204e-9763-5bdc-a87e-7d7366f4d64e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-x}-2{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93840/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbb42246-9fb5-5412-bced-3cb75be5fceb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93840/selection/b2faf1ca059239c75b27e85c9643ddc4144a7d6daf577ac4beb6f0db9ab7fbab" :answer-field/choices ["q-93840/selection/dfa228bf3eb066b1b38aa83c5d04b6f7393e470663ace6a5123a0e7c76cef8f3" "q-93840/selection/10e187ac029f78b83799d5ef21c84839ff17365a8e1dd17d9e1406697e8da9d6" "q-93840/selection/60693dc123e7d308b27dc6cf4a82a6c74f361da754e33fe63c7ec26320871b29" "q-93840/selection/b2faf1ca059239c75b27e85c9643ddc4144a7d6daf577ac4beb6f0db9ab7fbab" "q-93840/selection/a86345bd9c6764497c7636561836dc928800e1ed8eafbc0dbb5fabacff26a9de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93840" :question/id #uuid "3ea3e699-8539-58fa-9dc2-07fc9097ea9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-93840" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=-2{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(x)=A{e}^{x}+Bx{e}^{x}-2{e}^{2x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=-2{e}^{2x},\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =A{e}^{0}+B(0){e}^{0}-2{e}^{2(0)} \\\\ 0 & =A-2 \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=A{e}^{x}+Bx{e}^{x}+B{e}^{x}-4{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =A{e}^{0}+B(0){e}^{0}+B{e}^{0}-4{e}^{2(0)} \\\\ 0 & =A+B-4 \\\\ 0 & =2+B-4 \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A=2$ and $B=2,$ we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny=2{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}-2{e}^{2x}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93840/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "749a2a49-4181-5be7-b5ef-3e5f8d82219f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93840"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8108/selection/961b0059213745559f5313b37e6f67c4828fb12f6fd16ed49e2e009629eee3aa" :answer/id #uuid "0c4088f4-fce9-5681-b090-4fed673a1c49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8108/selection/5ca44ebb9a312a3f895feb799d3e6334f621183db7181894bdf072f37e583448" :answer/id #uuid "3aef229d-b47c-5261-a07b-127d811e5ec2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4{e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-3{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8108/selection/f3de47864b3fe0010c2de1a4b62cf1a1f658f7e438f7c86def35949970696ade" :answer/id #uuid "057f689b-687d-561f-8765-3f174bafeb13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4{e}^{-3x+\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8108/selection/24872f4b6d40bf36b02c04da44feed7bb32b5ebbd3bb3724aafcd03e53b33812" :answer/id #uuid "b56ac430-084f-532f-a4c5-d2f01f4efbf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-3x+\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+3{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8108/selection/7205de7d0cc2278ac1b048fb6c4a8c1866f44fe2ac3a33ee0eb843b08127f3ec" :answer/id #uuid "5af595e9-1461-566f-a4b1-b57e53c5559e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4{e}^{-3x+\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-3{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8108/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d6934a9-c07a-5561-920e-e9a92cfb5478" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8108/selection/7205de7d0cc2278ac1b048fb6c4a8c1866f44fe2ac3a33ee0eb843b08127f3ec" :answer-field/choices ["q-8108/selection/961b0059213745559f5313b37e6f67c4828fb12f6fd16ed49e2e009629eee3aa" "q-8108/selection/5ca44ebb9a312a3f895feb799d3e6334f621183db7181894bdf072f37e583448" "q-8108/selection/f3de47864b3fe0010c2de1a4b62cf1a1f658f7e438f7c86def35949970696ade" "q-8108/selection/24872f4b6d40bf36b02c04da44feed7bb32b5ebbd3bb3724aafcd03e53b33812" "q-8108/selection/7205de7d0cc2278ac1b048fb6c4a8c1866f44fe2ac3a33ee0eb843b08127f3ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8108" :question/id #uuid "5718b8be-20aa-5d90-b245-2b6bfc4ed681" :question/math-academy-id "q-8108" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+10y=-6{e}^{-2x},\\,y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={e}^{-\\pi },\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-2{e}^{-\\pi }.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+10y=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +10=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +10 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +9)-9+10 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda +3 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-3\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c}(x) & ={e}^{-3x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $-6{e}^{-2x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $-2$, which is not the root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {e}^{-2x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\alpha {e}^{-2x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=4\\alpha {e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\alpha {e}^{-2x}+6(-2\\alpha {e}^{-2x})+10(\\alpha {e}^{-2x}) & =-6{e}^{-2x} \\\\ (4-12+10)\\alpha {e}^{-2x} & =-6{e}^{-2x} \\\\ 2\\alpha  & =-6 \\\\ \\alpha  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-3{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-3x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-3{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants $P$ and $Q.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={e}^{-\\pi }$ into the general solution gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q{e}^{-3\\pi /2}-3{e}^{-\\pi } & ={e}^{-\\pi } \\\\ Q{e}^{-3\\pi /2} & =4{e}^{-\\pi } \\\\ Q & =4{e}^{\\pi /2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-2{e}^{-\\pi }.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=(Q-3P){e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-(P+3Q){e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6{e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-2{e}^{-\\pi }$ into the above gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(P+3Q){e}^{-3\\pi /2}+6{e}^{-\\pi } & =-2{e}^{-\\pi } \\\\ -(P+12{e}^{\\pi /2}){e}^{-3\\pi /2} & =-8{e}^{-\\pi } \\\\ -P{e}^{-3\\pi /2}-12{e}^{-\\pi } & =-8{e}^{-\\pi } \\\\ -P{e}^{-3\\pi /2} & =4{e}^{-\\pi } \\\\ P & =-4{e}^{\\pi /2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $P=-4{e}^{\\pi /2}$ and $Q=4{e}^{\\pi /2}.$\n\nWe substitute this into the general particular integral and find that the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(-4{e}^{\\pi /2}){e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(4{e}^{\\pi /2}){e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3{e}^{-2x} \\\\ y & =4{e}^{-3x+\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-3{e}^{-2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-8108/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "749a2a49-4181-5be7-b5ef-3e5f8d82219f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8108"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93691/selection/b8e3a08faa828c8cd87d7f9a2a8ae74bbcceb895286aab0093c295351b0d1983" :answer/id #uuid "d186b83b-140f-5608-8c09-4c15a8a2a8fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-3x}+4x{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93691/selection/1f77a3aab2ad56c6c18c3073a72aa95f21a514471f5d43170eca61d8b94f3d24" :answer/id #uuid "1bbe1e30-668f-5d83-a487-2fef4173e3ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-3x}+2{e}^{-2x}+4x{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93691/selection/b0d7b470d86deed50db3d07687e925772c2634d3868392a88c66849a3c35abb9" :answer/id #uuid "d3db79fe-8a63-55bb-a169-856038b215d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-3x}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}+4x{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93691/selection/bb5e49efe9e9f69a3383e068881afebae61389c97cf3c1fe14bb2fa4432a74fb" :answer/id #uuid "400b1c39-5a28-50bf-91b4-91220398b893" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}+4x{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93691/selection/db7bbda07cc6b3a291ced0afdedf7ffd3aa281c021b1775b625d6e0600aa8549" :answer/id #uuid "c085448b-3cea-5c1c-a2b9-3c22978c8f31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-3x}-2{e}^{2x}+4{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93691/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b533751f-14ae-5d39-be16-eb6ba3e10f8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93691/selection/b8e3a08faa828c8cd87d7f9a2a8ae74bbcceb895286aab0093c295351b0d1983" :answer-field/choices ["q-93691/selection/b8e3a08faa828c8cd87d7f9a2a8ae74bbcceb895286aab0093c295351b0d1983" "q-93691/selection/1f77a3aab2ad56c6c18c3073a72aa95f21a514471f5d43170eca61d8b94f3d24" "q-93691/selection/b0d7b470d86deed50db3d07687e925772c2634d3868392a88c66849a3c35abb9" "q-93691/selection/bb5e49efe9e9f69a3383e068881afebae61389c97cf3c1fe14bb2fa4432a74fb" "q-93691/selection/db7bbda07cc6b3a291ced0afdedf7ffd3aa281c021b1775b625d6e0600aa8549"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93691" :question/id #uuid "0b976d07-2159-5a25-8c79-4392e1bd3d72" :question/math-academy-id "q-93691" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6y=4{e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(x)=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{-2x}+4x{e}^{-2x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6y=4{e}^{-2x},\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =A{e}^{-3(0)}+B{e}^{-2(0)}+4(0){e}^{-2(0)} \\\\ 1 & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A{e}^{-3x}-2B{e}^{-2x}-8x{e}^{-2x}+4{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=1$ into the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-3A{e}^{-3(0)}-2B{e}^{-2(0)}-8(0){e}^{-2(0)}+4{e}^{-2(0)} \\\\ 1 & =-3A-2B+4 \\\\ -3 & =-3A-2B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=1 \\\\ -3A-2B=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=1,B=0.$\n\nFinally, since $A=1$ and $B=0,$ we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-3x}+4x{e}^{-2x}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93691/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "749a2a49-4181-5be7-b5ef-3e5f8d82219f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93691"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8100"] :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-12y=10{e}^{2x},\\,y(0)=0,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(0)=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-12y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -12 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-3$ or $\\lambda =4$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $10{e}^{2x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $2$, which is not the root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {e}^{2x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha {e}^{2x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=4\\alpha {e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\alpha {e}^{2x}-2\\alpha {e}^{2x}-12(\\alpha {e}^{2x}) & =10{e}^{2x} \\\\ \\alpha (4-2-12){e}^{2x} & =10{e}^{2x} \\\\ -10\\alpha {e}^{2x} & =10{e}^{2x} \\\\ -10\\alpha  & =10 \\\\ \\alpha  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{4x}-{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nLet us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=0$ into the general solution gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B-1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=2.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A{e}^{-3x}+4B{e}^{4x}-2{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=2$ into the above gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3A+4B-2 & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=1 \\\\ -3A+4B=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=0,B=1.$\n\nWe substitute this into the general particular integral and find that the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{4x}-{e}^{2x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6609"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} + \\frac{\\textrm{d} y}{\\textrm{d} x} - 2y = 20 e ^ {3x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the complementary solution by solving the associated homogeneous ODE. Since the roots of the characteristic equation are $\\lambda = 1, -2,$ we get\n\n$$\ny_c  = Ae^{x} + Be^{- 2 x}.\n$$\n\nSecond, we find a particular solution of the inhomogeneous ODE. We see that the right-hand side is $20e^{3x},$ and $e^{3x}$ is not a term in the complementary solution, so we assume that a particular solution takes the form \n\n$$\ny_p = \\alpha e^{3x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha$ is a constant to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of $y_p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}y_p}{\\textrm{d}x} = 3 \\alpha e ^{3x},\n\\quad \\frac{\\textrm{d}^2y_p}{\\textrm{d}x^2} = 9  \\alpha e ^{3x}.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha,$  we substitute the derivatives into the original ODE and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9\\alpha {e}^{3x}+3\\alpha {e}^{3x}-2\\alpha {e}^{3x} & =20{e}^{3x} \\\\ \\alpha (9+3-2){e}^{3x} & =20{e}^{3x} \\\\ 10\\alpha {e}^{3x} & =20{e}^{3x} \\\\ 10\\alpha  & =20 \\\\ \\alpha  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is \n\n$$\ny_p = 2e^{3x}\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={y}_{c}+{y}_{p} \\\\  & =A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{-2x}+2{e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6610"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/4652a17e8836f9ea84df971537f3c0df1f5ccd2b2dfd7d8d9615ef69a775b972.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the complementary solution by solving the associated homogeneous ODE. Since the roots of the characteristic equation are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/bb796871deb9ebb6ff0ac3c98715a74275b8957374753a1bfed998898de136f8.png) we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/fbd5028588b1b3639ae465a5904a49e354da5f77ae0224b398666449dcfd809b.png)\n\nSecond, we find a particular solution of the inhomogeneous ODE. We see that the right-hand side is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/4d6d063a30dc8f4bab52eab0764e8dee217ddd74055d79cae2bcca34e46ca45f.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/df86a6554579076b0783330da9971ee6ac847ce0d7615c81da959cc197372021.png) is a term in the complementary solution, so we assume that a particular solution takes the form \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/187230e4c3f0192e65cb84e69fa12ece83467ae67ca3f73f09ae636d8eb7daad.png)\n\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/13751f284d6fa34631cd1eb362665db0f1e29de98a1539e514009e7c5034e855.png) is a constant to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/6316c498377eadd30922f7f5ef6cfa1015cb3c059349bccf2aec7ca52ea5356e.png) we get\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/955d1d9ea20426db629258e32703eda1f724e0787bedc68c653eaa684a997f02.png)\n\nTo find the value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/07f02913cce959d6fde7770ff94b1fbab15d24d8c7f7ee5c8cba48873d955f86.png)  we substitute the derivatives into the original ODE and get\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/0770a9b23e24c99631cdbc12378388ff089585206f0aea21ebfb3f65217cd4a2.png)\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/67180bb752c7046f8b83aadacd7753bed9d827516c4f1930b341873b5399951e.png)\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/dbf2415e9f21a606aa92b6e26582cc1790470343346e967a0ff621c678560fd6.png)\n\nand the general solution is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065386/assets/a197e920c5e9c7d6b16fffcd7955fe07a212b92fb50636feae2c771f91a68f8a.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6611"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} - 6\\frac{\\textrm{d} y}{\\textrm{d} x} + 9y = e ^{3x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the complementary solution by solving the associated homogeneous ODE. Since the characteristic equation has a single repeated root $\\lambda = 3,$ the complementary solution is\n\n$$\ny_c(x) = Ae^{3x} + Bxe^{3x}.\n$$\n\nSecond, we find a particular solution of the inhomogeneous ODE. We see that the right-hand side is $e^{3x},$ and $e^{3x}$ and $xe^{3x}$ are both terms in the complementary solution, so we assume that a particular solution takes the form \n\n$$\ny_p = \\alpha x^2e ^ {3x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha$ is a constant to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of $y_p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =(3{x}^{2}+2x)\\alpha {e}^{3x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=(9{x}^{2}+12x+2)\\alpha {e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $y_p$, $y'_p$ and $y_p''$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9{x}^{2}+12x+2)\\alpha {e}^{3x}-6(3{x}^{2}+2x)\\alpha {e}^{3x}+9\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{3x} & ={e}^{3x} \\\\ (9{x}^{2}+12x+2-18{x}^{2}-12x+9{x}^{2})\\alpha {e}^{3x} & ={e}^{3x} \\\\ 2\\alpha {e}^{3x} & ={e}^{3x} \\\\ 2\\alpha  & =1 \\\\ \\alpha  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny_p(x) = \\dfrac 1 2x^2 e ^{3x},\n$$\n\nand the general solution is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={y}_{c}+{y}_{p} \\\\  & =A{e}^{3x}+Bx{e}^{3x}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6787"] :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} - 6\\frac{\\textrm{d} y}{\\textrm{d} x} + 9y = e ^{3x}\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\nAe^{3 x} + Bxe^{3 x} + \\dfrac 1 2 x ^2 e^{3 x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} - 6\\frac{\\textrm{d} y}{\\textrm{d} x} + 9y = e ^{3x}, \\qquad y(0) = 2 , \\ \\ y'(0) = 1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =A{e}^{0}+B(0){e}^{0}+\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}{e}^{0} \\\\ 2 & =A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=3A{e}^{3x}+B{e}^{3x}+3Bx{e}^{3x}+x{e}^{3x}+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}{e}^{3x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y'(0)=1$ into the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =3A{e}^{0}+B{e}^{0}+3B(0){e}^{0}+0{e}^{0}+\\frac{3}{2}(0)^{2}{e}^{0} \\\\ 1 & =3A+B \\\\ 1 & =3(2)+B \\\\ -5 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A=2$ and $B=-5,$ we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2{e}^{3x}-5x{e}^{3x}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
